1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,380
First of all, let me thank you all for coming to this public meeting

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:07,130
to discuss the future of our town.

3
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:12,330
Our first speaker is Shona Ferguson, from Barford town council. Shona.

4
00:00:12,330 --> 00:00:16,034
Thank you. First I'll briefly give you some background information,

5
00:00:16,034 --> 00:00:20,850
then I'll be asking you for your comments on developments in the town.

6
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:24,020
Well, as you don't need me to tell you

7
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:27,791
Barford has changed a great deal in the last 50 years.

8
00:00:27,791 --> 00:00:30,220
These are some of the main changes.

9
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:34,880
Fifty years ago, buses linked virtually every part of the town

10
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,850
and the neighbouring towns and villages.

11
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:38,912
Most people used them frequently,

12
00:00:38,912 --> 00:00:45,510
but not now, because the bus companies concentrate on just the routes that attract most passengers.

13
00:00:45,510 --> 00:00:49,280
So parts of the town are no longer served by buses.

14
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:56,930
Even replacing old uncomfortable buses with smart new ones has had little impact on passenger numbers.

15
00:00:56,930 --> 00:01:00,118
It's sometimes said that bus fares are too high,

16
00:01:00,118 --> 00:01:02,960
but in relation to average incomes

17
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,140
fares are not much higher than they were 50 years ago.

18
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,680
Changes in the road network are affecting the town.

19
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:14,820
The centre was recently closed to traffic on a trial basis

20
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:17,340
making it much safer for pedestrians.

21
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:20,020
The impact of this is being measured.

22
00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:25,342
The new cycle paths, separating bikes from cars in most main roads,

23
00:01:25,342 --> 00:01:28,520
are being used far more than was expected

24
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:31,550
reducing traffic and improving air quality.

25
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:35,995
And although the council's attempts to have a bypass constructed have failed,

26
00:01:35,995 --> 00:01:40,810
we haven't given up hope of persuading the government to change its mind.

27
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:45,010
Shopping in the town centre has changed over the years.

28
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:49,390
Many of us can remember when the town was crowded with people going shopping.

29
00:01:49,390 --> 00:01:52,444
Numbers have been falling for several years,

30
00:01:52,444 --> 00:01:57,680
despite efforts to attract shoppers, for instance by opening new car parks.

31
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:02,560
Some people combine shopping with visits to the town's restaurants and cafes.

32
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:06,620
Most shops are small independent stores, which is good

33
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:08,945
but many people prefer to use supermarkets

34
00:02:08,945 --> 00:02:12,340
and department stores in nearby large towns

35
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:15,330
as there are so few well-known chain stores here.

36
00:02:15,330 --> 00:02:18,540
Turning now to medical facilities

37
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:22,416
the town is served by family doctors in several medical practices -

38
00:02:22,416 --> 00:02:27,730
fewer than 50 years ago, but each catering for far more patients.

39
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,920
Our hospital closed 15 years ago

40
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:34,070
which means journeys to other towns are unavoidable.

41
00:02:34,070 --> 00:02:38,340
On the other hand, there are more dentists than there used to be.

42
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:42,820
Employment patterns have changed, along with almost everything else.

43
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:45,620
The number of schools and colleges has increased

44
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:48,000
making that the main employment sector.

45
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,580
Services, such as website design and accountancy

46
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:53,541
have grown in importance, and surprisingly,

47
00:02:53,541 --> 00:03:00,360
perhaps, manufacturing hasn't seen the decline that has affected it in other parts of the country.

48
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:08,820
Now I'll very quickly outline current plans for some of the town's facilities

49
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,230
before asking for your comments.

50
00:03:11,230 --> 00:03:17,940
As you'll know if you regularly use the car park at the railway station, it's usually full.

51
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:24,340
The railway company applied for permission to replace it with a multi-storey car park, but that was refused.

52
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,916
Instead, the company has bought some adjoining land,

53
00:03:26,916 --> 00:03:30,780
and this will be used to increase the number of parking spaces.

54
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:33,820
The Grand, the old cinema in the high street,

55
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:38,550
will close at the end of the year, and reopen on a different site.

56
00:03:38,550 --> 00:03:41,240
You've probably seen the building under construction.

57
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:44,721
The plan is to have three screens with fewer seats,

58
00:03:44,721 --> 00:03:48,550
rather than just the one large auditorium in the old cinema.

59
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:52,700
I expect many of you shop in the indoor market.

60
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:55,586
It's become more and more shabby- looking,

61
00:03:55,586 --> 00:04:00,120
and because of fears about safety, it was threatened with demolition.

62
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:05,635
The good news is that it will close for six weeks to be made safe and redecorated,

63
00:04:05,635 --> 00:04:08,230
and the improved building will open in July.

64
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:10,880
Lots of people use the library

65
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:14,490
including school and college students who go there to study.

66
00:04:14,490 --> 00:04:20,890
The council has managed to secure funding to keep the library open later into the evening, twice a week.

67
00:04:20,890 --> 00:04:24,440
We would like to enlarge the building in the not-too-distant future

68
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,310
but this is by no means definite.

69
00:04:27,310 --> 00:04:31,920
There's no limit on access to the nature reserve on the edge of town

70
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:34,360
and this will continue to be the case.

71
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:39,440
What will change, though, is that the council will no longer be in charge of the area.

72
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:46,720
Instead it will become the responsibility of a national body that administers most nature reserves in the country.
